re's necrosword belongs to  null the symbiote god before the thor  villain gets his claws on it in donny  kate's venom number four the villain  recounts his origin to eddie brock  explaining that billions of years in the  past he lived alone in a void that  quickly became the battleground for a  celestial war because they invade null's  empty kingdom he conjures a sword out of  the void and beheads a celestial before  turning its severed head into a forge  where he makes the necrosword a  permanent weapon essentially it's a  blade of living darkness that also traps  the soul of anything it kills inside it  because null is a key part of the venom  mythology it seems likely that sony has  the rights to use null however it sees  fit even though the studio bought the  rights to spider-man and his related  characters a number of years before the  villain debuted in the comics as such  this is probably why co-writers taika  waititi and jennifer kaden robinson use  an ambiguous figure rather than  acknowledging the null of it all it's  unclear if the two studios could or  would strike a deal for null to appear  in the mcu but it seems far more likely  that he'd show up in a future venom film  with tom hardy's symbiotic anti-hero  first  all of us  [Music]  it's also worth pointing out that the  necro sword is also called the all black  and it's actually the very first  symbiote yes the sword is technically  alive what's interesting is that it also  cloaks null in a set of black armor with  a red insignia on the front which gives  the immortal villain a terrifying look  so the dead knight in the opening of  thor love and thunder clearly a nod to  the necrosword's origins without getting  into the messy implications of null  himself being in the mcu gore briefly  meets null in thor god of thunder number  six where the villain reveals his origin  to an imprisoned volstag the issue  explains that gore is exiled from his  tribe for his rage against the gods and  shortly after he stumbles on an armored  null fighting a golden god in the desert  although their fight has ended in a  stalemate because they've impaled each  other all black quickly jumps into  gore's hand as a dagger and he uses it  to kill the golden god in revenge for  the deaths of his mother his wife and  his daughter over the years that's not  too far from the film's opening where  gore stumbles into rapu's realm and uses  the discarded weapon to kill his former  idol the necrosword symbiote abilities  are a huge part of the film too as gore  brings monstrous black berserkers out of  the abyss inside the necrosword to  plague the asgardians and steal the  children of new asgard when the villain  kills several gods in thor god of  thunder number 1 and number 3 he leaves  a few berserkers behind as sentries to  slaughter anyone investigating their  deaths taika ytt clearly did his  homework  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  thor love and thunder are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

